This message was triggered by a recent posting in this newsgroup
inquiring about a free Tru64 server. This is not it but it may help.

As you are probably aware of we developed CHARON-AXP which is software
that creates the Alpha hardware environment in a regular Intel/AMD
based computer. We have a set of products that provide a quick and
easy replacement of your AlphaServer systems. These are commercially
available and as part of that program we have released a freeware
version for personal use: PersonalAlpha. This runs on a standard,
Windows based computer and many of your OpenVMS peers use it to run
OpenVMS on their laptops. For testing, development or just for fun.

Recently we released version 1.2 of PersonalAlpha which includes
support for Tru64 and that could make it interesting for the
participants of this forum. It gives you 4 disks, 128 MB of memory and
1 Ethernet, but most important: it can run on your laptop.

When you are interested look on www.personalalpha.com for more
information and a free download. We also invite you to participate in
the PersonalAlpha form (link on the same page) where you can post
questions and opinions.

