Barani, this is correct, we implemented the SRM console, especially
since Tru64 requires this. So the bootflags settings can be done in
the SRM console and are removed from the user interface.
Please enter the requested data for disks and Ethernet in the user
interface en click start. You will see the console with the >>>
prompt.

Occasionaly communication between the user interface and the emulator
is prohibited by older firewall/antivirus software nesting itself in
the TCPIP Stack, often the software is still there even when you
deinstalled the original. When the terminal emulator doesn't appear or
drops away again after a short time, you may suffer this problem.
Cleaning up the stack is the solution for this. Please contact us if
you experience this problem. The problem is also described in the
PersonalAlpha forum.

